    },
    "S2_new_span": {
      "id": "S2",
      "byte_start": 41732,
      "byte_end_exclusive": 44201,
      "line_start": 901,
      "line_end": 926,
      "bytes": 2469,
      "sha256": "f21ccf155c6b20a1d42f7e3f7b3f00c0ef5b86c187ac4d8bb8879fe0a7da7197",
      "text": "\n\n\\par\\smallskip\n\\begingroup\n\\footnotesize\n\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.08}\n\\setlength{\\tabcolsep}{3pt}\n\\noindent\\textbf{Frozen Bitbrains data protocol.}\\par\\smallskip\n\\noindent\\begin{tabularx}{\\linewidth}{@{}p{0.18\\linewidth}Y@{}}\n\\toprule\nItem & Definition or actual per-VM window counts \\\\\n\\midrule\nQualification & Fixed 11-column schema; finite integer Unix-second timestamps in $[10^9,2\\times10^9)$, strictly increasing; finite nonnegative CPU labels; at least 3,000 post-first-day records and 50 complete source windows for each horizon. Every $H/K$ case requires exactly $K$ support windows and at least 80/60/200 validation/check/test windows. These predicates yield 1,082 eligible VMs before identity selection. \\\\\nTimeline & Source uses records in $[t_0,t_0+86{,}400\\,\\mathrm{s})$, where $t_0$ is each VM's first timestamp (observed first-to-last span 86,107 s); target uses the first 3,000 native records at/after that cutoff (observed spans 899,799--903,397 s). Support contains $96+H+K-1$ raw records; remaining records follow normalized $0.2{:}0.1{:}0.1$ validation/check/test allocation, with floors then largest remainders and earlier-segment tie priority. \\\\\nChannels & Ten raw fields: CPU cores, capacity, MHz usage and percent usage; memory capacity/usage; disk read/write and network received/transmitted throughput. Add trailing-five CPU mean and first difference, their 12 corresponding validity masks, and preceding elapsed seconds/1,200. Invalid inputs use causal forward fill from initial zero; masks retain invalidity. Fill, mean, difference and gap state restart at every raw role boundary. \\\\\n$H=1,K=10$ & $(10,\\;1{,}351,\\;628,\\;627)$ \\\\\n$H=1,K=20$ & $(20,\\;1{,}346,\\;625,\\;625)$ \\\\\n$H=4,K=10$ & $(10,\\;1{,}346,\\;624,\\;624)$ \\\\\n$H=4,K=20$ & $(20,\\;1{,}342,\\;621,\\;621)$ \\\\\nFrozen entry & \\href{https://github.com/w924871681/paper-code-DT-Twin/releases/download/evidence-full-20261013/MSA_DTI_R5_Bitbrains_ResearchAssets_PUBLIC_PATHSAFE_20261013.zip}{Public protocol asset}: \\path{code/experiments/r4_r5/bitbrains_data.py} and \\path{bitbrains/data/bitbrains_dataset_manifest.json}. \\\\\n\\bottomrule\n\\end{tabularx}\n\\par\\smallskip\n\\noindent Count order is support, validation, calibration check, and held-out test; counts are constant within the corresponding VM groups. Validation applies to calibration and held-out cases; development-fixed uses support/check only. These are windows, which may share label endpoints.\n\\endgroup\n\\par\\smallskip"
    },
